<title>USA: Rouse files for $400 mln debt, stock shelf.</title>
<headline>Rouse files for $400 mln debt, stock shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rouse Co said Friday it filed a shelf registration with the Securities and Exchange Commission to sell up to $400 million in common stock and preferred stock and debt securities.</p>
<p>Net proceeds will be used for general corporate purposes, the filing said.</p>
<p>Rouse, based in Columbia, Md., is engaged in the ownership, management, acquisition and development of income-producing and other real estate in the United States.</p>
</text>
